{
 "about": "LST's list fixture (tests/driver/p6_leftlist.py; desktop-design-5-6 2.20 to 2.23). Every *_at time is a local wall-clock time on its day around 2026-10-18 (the anchor); the driver moves the days so the anchor day is today. Today: a chat that keeps working (spin), one the list starts as working and whose first read says it finished (done, so it turns unread), one waiting for permission, one in the background, a ready one, an untitled one and one with a picture (a view tool's image); yesterday one; then 24 older notes so the list scrolls. GET servers is G-18's answer: a named job's port (web :8000), a job holding two ports (dev: node :5173, esbuild :5174) and a plain process's port with no name (8100). At 4 s another app creates the chat fresh, which has no record to read, so it stays unknown.",
